    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**Issue 1: `src/eval/index.test.js` - toxicity.score was 0 instead of 1**\n- Problem: `toxicityMetric` was receiving `references` as its second parameter (from `runEvaluations` calling `metric(outputs, references)`), but the function treated it as `bannedTerms`, causing it to incorrectly flag the test outputs as toxic.\n- Solution: Changed `DEFAULT_METRICS` to wrap `toxicityMetric` in an object with an `evaluate` method that only passes `outputs` to the function, ignoring the `references` parameter.\n\n**Issue 2: `src/finetune/governance.test.js` - APPROVAL_STATUSES was undefined**\n- Problem: The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only imported from schema.js and not re-exported.\n- Solution: Added named exports for all schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) in the finetune index.js file.\n\nBoth fixes maintain full backward compatibility with existing public APIs.",
